  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m now breaking down the user\'s request. I\'m focusing on identifying the core entities: HQ, client, owner of the app, registered stores, the consumer, public pages, and the marketplace. I need to understand the relationships and processes involved in this system. I am moving towards identifying the system entities.\n\n\n**Defining Core System Elements**\n\nI\'m now identifying the key system elements based on the directives provided. I see a clear separation between the HQ, client (operating system - OS), and the consumer. The HQ, I\'m understanding, is managed by the app owner and centralizes everything possible. The OS pertains to registered stores, while the final consumer uses public pages, the catalog, and the marketplace. I am also gathering fundamental agent rules.\n\n\n**Defining System Agents**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the roles and responsibilities of each agent within the described system. The SaaS SuperAdmin (Founder/Platform) has comprehensive control, managing stores, metrics, subscriptions, commissions, fleet management, routing, gateways, marketplace moderation, and feature flags. The OS (Client OS/Shop/Desktop) is for registered stores, handling POS, kitchen displays, inventory, finances, integrations, and local configurations. The final consumer accesses public pages, store catalogs, and the marketplace.\n\n\n"
