    thinking: "**Examining File References**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/app/components/os-windows/admin-hub-window.ts` and `src/app/components/client-os.ts` to examine the related code. Specifically, I need to check line 529 of `client-os.ts`. It seems to provide details about an admin hub section, with a label, title and icon.\n\n\n**Clarifying Ownership and Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core concept: \"Gabinete do Dono\" is the **HQ Central**, managed by the **App Owner**. It handles everything possible in the ecosystem. I\'m focusing on defining the scope of this HQ, including tenant provisioning, commission governance, SaaS plan management, and MDM fleet control. It needs to be super clear on these responsibilities.\n\n\n**Defining HQ Central Boundaries**\n\nI\'m now separating concerns between the \"HQ Central\" and the \"Store OS\". My understanding is sharpening: the HQ handles the big picture\342\200\224regional portals, global CRM, cloud infrastructure, and auditing. The App Owner is purely executive, not involved in front-of-house operations. The Store OS, owned by the registered store, is for day-to-day operations like point-of-sale. This separation is crucial.\n\n\n**Delineating Operational Scope**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the scope for the registered store\'s operational tasks. This encompasses barcode scanning, inventory management, and financial reconciliation. It also includes managing tables and dining areas, kitchen display systems, and logistics with own fleet. I must ensure the final consumer and the app owner won\'t directly engage with these functions. This is core to the store\'s operations.\n\n\n**Refining Public Marketplace Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how customers discover and interact with stores. I\'m thinking about the digital menu and catalog (`/p/:id`), which includes item selection, delivery fee calculation, and checkout. I\'m also considering real-time public order tracking. I need to check architectural docs, specifically `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `HQ_CENTRAL_DOCUMENTATION.md`, and `BUGS_AND_SOLUTIONS.md`, to ensure the customer-facing aspects are clearly defined and differentiated from the store\'s operations and the HQ Central\'s management functions.\n\n\n**Clarifying System Hierarchies**\n\nI\'m now making explicit descriptions and labels in `ecosystem-switcher.ts`, clarifying the roles of \"HQ CENTRAL,\" \"STORE OS,\" \"MARKETPLACE & CAT\303\201LOGO,\" \"LOG\303\215STICA,\" and \"COMANDA DIGITAL.\" I\'m ensuring alignment and checking the login card labels and headers in `login-bancada.ts` to reflect the ownership and access tiers, with roles for App Owner and Registered Company/Store.\n\n\n"
