  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Terminology Mismatch**\n\nI\'ve homed in on lines 112 and 200 of `hq-documentation-modal.ts`. It seems there\'s a terminology mismatch. \"Lojista\" is used in two different contexts (Client OS and Empresa), which could be the source of the confusion the user mentioned regarding \"hq central.\" I\'m currently assessing the implications of these discrepancies.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on the user\'s explicit distinction between \"HQ Central\" and the store\'s OS. It\'s becoming clear that the confusion stems from conflating the app owner\'s management system (HQ Central) with the individual store\'s operating system. The user wants to ensure the store OS remains separate, accessible only to the store, while HQ Central manages everything *globally*. The consumer only interacts with public facing content.\n\n\n**Defining Architectural Principles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring that the architectural principles are clearly and consistently articulated throughout the application and documentation. I\'m checking `HQ_CENTRAL_DOCUMENTATION.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `BUGS_AND_SOLUTIONS.md` and the UI (Switcher, Login, HQ Central, Store OS, Documentation modal, and Header) to harmonize terminology. My goal is to clearly differentiate \"Gabinete do Dono do App \342\200\242 Gest\303\243o Global de Lojas, Split, MDM e Marketplace\" for HQ Central, \"Sistema Operacional da Loja Cadastrada (Store OS) \342\200\242 PDV Caixa, Mesas, KDS, Estoque e Finan\303\247as\" for Store OS, and \"P\303\241ginas P\303\272blicas do Consumidor \342\200\242 Cat\303\241logo da Loja & Marketplace Regional\" for the Public Customer sphere. I\'m also ensuring the owner\'s experience in HQ Central avoids any features related to store-level operations to prevent confusion.\n\n\n"
