  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Build Process**\n\nI\'m currently observing an `ng build` process, specifically for an SSR application, which is taking approximately 20-30 seconds. I recall the `compile_applet` script throwing an error \"Script not found \'build\'\" in the past when invoked from an incorrect location or if a previous build was still active. I\'m investigating how this build time impacts overall performance and deployment strategies.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Linter**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that `ng lint` completed successfully, with all files passing the linting process. My focus has now shifted to reviewing necessary updates and implementations. Specifically, I am going to re-articulate the Tripartite Architecture within `ARCHITECTURE.md` to ensure clarity and precision, directly addressing key principles to differentiate the HQ Central, the Store OS, and the End Consumer\'s access points.\n\n\n**Clarifying Key Architectural Concepts**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into refining the documentation, specifically focusing on the distinctions between the HQ Central, the Store OS, and the End Consumer\'s access points. I\'m reinforcing the definitions in sections 1 and 2 of `RAL_DOCUMENTATION.md` and clarifying that HQ Central is strictly for app owners, free of any store-level operations. Furthermore, I\'ve added a bug, BUG-025, to `BUGS_AND_SOLUTIONS.md` which details an ambiguity in the architecture, stemming from confusing terminology. The solution, which I\'ve now documented, involves harmonizing the taxonomy across the documents and UI and ensuring clear visual and conceptual segregation. The \'Store OS\' and \'HQ central\' are now defined.\n\n\n**Refining Terminology Consistency**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on ensuring absolute clarity and consistency in terminology. I\'ve meticulously reviewed the descriptions for each system: the HQ Central (Gabinete do Dono), the Store OS (Sistema Operacional da Loja), the Marketplace (P\303\241ginas P\303\272blicas), 3EAT Entregas (App de Log\303\255stica), and the Gar\303\247om (Comanda Digital) app. My aim is to eliminate all potential for ambiguity, directly by updating labels within the application\'s login flow, specifically `src/app/components/login-bancada.ts`, ensuring the Portuguese copy accurately reflects these revised definitions and descriptions.\n\n\n**Updating System Nomenclature**\n\nI\'m currently updating the system descriptions, focusing on clarity in application labels and architectural summaries. I\'m incorporating detailed explanations within `hq-central.ts` and `hq-documentation-modal.ts` to differentiate the \"Gabinete Central do Dono do App\" from the \"Sistema Operacional da Loja (Store OS)\". Additionally, I\'m modifying the terminal widget title in `client-os.ts` to reflect either \"SISTEMA DA EMPRESA CADASTRADA (STORE OS)\" or \"Suporte Remoto do Dono do App\", depending on access. Next, I\'ll update `src/app/components/shared/ecosystem`.\n\n\n"
